---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy - DSUI" description="How the DSUI website and software handle your data.">
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas px-6 py-24 text-foreground">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <a href="/" class="text-sm text-copy-subtle transition-colors hover:text-foreground">← DSUI</a>
      <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-copy-subtle">Draft - to be reviewed before launch.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">This website</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-copy">
        With your permission we measure which pages are visited and which links are clicked, using PostHog (EU).
        Nothing is loaded and no cookie is set until you accept measurement in the cookie banner.
        You can change your choice at any time with "Cookie settings" in the footer.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Self-hosted DSUI</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-copy">
        The open source server sends a small anonymous event on start and once a day: version, operating system, a random install id and counts of services per adapter type.
        It never sends hostnames, credentials, queries or your IP address.
        Turn it off with <code>DSUI_TELEMETRY=off</code> or <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code>.
        See the <a class="underline" href="/docs/telemetry">telemetry page</a> for the exact fields.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">DSUI Cloud</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-copy">
        The managed product records product usage events against your account to improve it.
        Its own privacy terms will be linked from the sign-in page.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
